\tag{fnip}
\taxon{Remark}
\title{A bounded remainder}
\date{2026-11-27}

\p{The integral in \ref{fnip-0092} is computed in the coordinate on
the [center manifold](fnip-0059). [Topological equivalence](fnip-0082)
keeps the orbits and loses this dependence on time, as
\ref{fnip-0083} records.}

\p{Outside a neighborhood of the fold, the time spent on the closed
curve stays bounded as the current approaches the fold. The square-root
law therefore describes the period near onset.
\citet{p. 60}{ermentrout2010mathematical} records that the
frequency becomes arbitrarily low as the current approaches the fold,
and Exercise 8 on p. 72 asks for the square-root law.}
